Theorem L-1: Lattice join commutativity

  Preconditions:
    - a, b are AimsState elements per the canonical proof notation
      sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
    - join is the product-lattice componentwise join per Annex E §AIMS + §AIMS §3 L-1
    - Per-dimension joins per Annex E §AIMS §3.1 through §AIMS §3.7

  Soundness property:
    Forall a, b in AimsState. join(a, b) = join(b, a)

  Proof obligation:
    Componentwise per-dimension finite enumeration over the 7 carriers
    proves dim_join_d(x, y) = dim_join_d(y, x) for every (x, y) in the
    dimension's carrier squared. Product-lattice commutativity follows
    by the componentwise-lift lemma: if every dimension's join is
    commutative, the product join (defined componentwise) is commutative.

    Per-dimension carriers + sizes (pair counts = |carrier| ^ 2):
      Access {B, O} 2 => 4 pairs
      Consumption {empty, L, A, U} 4 => 16 pairs
      Cardinality {absent, 1, omega} 3 => 9 pairs
      Uniqueness {u, ms, s} 3 => 9 pairs
      Locality {bl, fl, ae, he, top} 5 => 25 pairs
      Shape {Phi, R_S, R_V, C, H} 5 => 25 pairs
      Effect 3-bit flag set 8 => 64 pairs

    Per-dimension argument:
      Access / Consumption / Cardinality / Uniqueness / Locality:
        max on a totally ordered carrier; max is commutative because
        max(x, y) selects the greater of the two and the predicate
        x >= y is decidable and totally ordered, so the selection is
        symmetric.
      Shape (flat lattice with Phi as TOP):
        join is case_analysis(x == y -> x; x != y -> Phi); both arms
        are symmetric in x and y (equality is symmetric; the unequal
        arm returns Phi regardless of order).
      Effect (componentwise OR on 3-bit flag product):
        OR on Bool is commutative; per-flag commutativity composes
        componentwise.

    Lift to product:
      join(a, b) = (dim_join_d(a_d, b_d))_d for d in 1..7
                 = (dim_join_d(b_d, a_d))_d for d in 1..7 (per-dim L-1)
                 = join(b, a)

    Sentinel handling per L-9: SCALAR is pre-filtered before any join
    invocation; canonicalize does not propagate SCALAR. Sentinels
    FRESH, CONSERVATIVE, ALL, NONE are concrete lattice values
    (instantiated 7-tuples) and obey componentwise commutativity.

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-dimension finite enumeration discharge per
        section_02::verify_l1_commutativity)
      monotonicity (validates the per-dimension joins used in L-1 are
        the same max/case_analysis/OR primitives whose monotonicity
        L-6 will discharge)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-02 lattice engine discharges L-1 via per-dimension finite enumeration over the 7 dimension carriers
